#: ../../source/docs/common-apm-navigation-extended-kalman-filter-overview.rst:5
#: 7609226f8bce4914a9a862718f30ec91
msgid "Extended Kalman Filter (EKF)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm-navigation-extended-kalman-filter-overview.rst:9
#: 4ae8ad015795493aaf63914a48f48411
msgid "An Extended Kalman Filter (EKF) algorithm is used to estimate vehicle position, velocity and angular orientation based on rate gyroscopes, accelerometer, compass, GPS, airspeed and barometric pressure measurements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm-navigation-extended-kalman-filter-overview.rst:14
#: d33022e67e414eef8f3befb9be9c142b
msgid "The advantage of the EKF over the simpler complementary filter algorithms (i.e. \"Inertial Nav\" or DCM), is that by fusing all available measurements it is better able to reject measurements with significant errors. This makes the vehicle less susceptible to faults that affect a single sensor. An EKF also enables measurements from optional sensors such as optical flow and laser range finders to be used to assist navigation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm-navigation-extended-kalman-filter-overview.rst:21
#: 9b4bba79a88a431f92d4947e3e4d8067
msgid "Current stable versions of ArduPilot use EKF3 as their primary attitude and position estimation source with DCM running quietly in the background. If the autopilot has two (or more) IMUs available, two EKF \"cores\" (i.e. two instances of the EKF) will run in parallel, each using a different IMU. At any one time, only the output from a single EKF core is ever used, that core being the one that reports the best health which is determined by the consistency of its sensor data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm-navigation-extended-kalman-filter-overview.rst:25
#: f2c8a3a3da414df28cb37202058e3d26
msgid "Most users should not need to modify any EKF parameters, but the information below provides some information on those parameters that are most commonly changed. More detailed information can be found on the :ref:`developer EKF wiki page <dev:extended-kalman-filter>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm-navigation-extended-kalman-filter-overview.rst:29
#: cc4fe6e10814452b9dbc496b7cd5f072
msgid "Should the EKF2 or EKF3 be used?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm-navigation-extended-kalman-filter-overview.rst:31
#: dd939ce1d86242da954390684f9f0e37
msgid "In general, we recommend users stick with the EKF3, which is now the default. In addition, 1MB autopilots only have this option due to space limitations. EKF2 can still be used but does not have many of the enhancements of EKF3 such as newer sensor sources including Beacons, Wheel Encoders and Visual Odometry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm-navigation-extended-kalman-filter-overview.rst:35
#: d16ef4dac97f4e79a741144f4147bc08
msgid "Choosing the EKF and number of cores"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm-navigation-extended-kalman-filter-overview.rst:37
#: 6ea738d3213741c9956f914a9dd6df2b
msgid ":ref:`AHRS_EKF_USE <dev:extended-kalman-filter_ahrs_ekf_use>`: set to \"1\" to use the EKF, \"0\" to use DCM for attitude control and ahrs dead reckoning (Plane) for position control.  In Copter this parameter is forced to \"1\" and cannot be changed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm-navigation-extended-kalman-filter-overview.rst:39
#: 84ea44387cf54904b864bf0dca6d90c3
msgid ":ref:`AHRS_EKF_TYPE <AHRS_EKF_TYPE>`: set to \"2\" to use EKF2 for attitude and position estimation, \"3\" for EKF3."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm-navigation-extended-kalman-filter-overview.rst:41
#: 9114b78573464da0aaa26785236f474e
msgid ":ref:`EK2_ENABLE <EK2_ENABLE>`, :ref:`EK3_ENABLE <EK3_ENABLE>`: set to \"1\" to enable the EKF2 and/or EKF3 respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm-navigation-extended-kalman-filter-overview.rst:43
#: 41020368ea6a419c82c82ea5cfce871c
msgid ":ref:`EK2_IMU_MASK <EK2_IMU_MASK>`, :ref:`EK3_IMU_MASK <EK3_IMU_MASK>`: a bitmask specifying which IMUs (i.e. accelerometer/gyro) to use.  An EKF \"core\" (i.e. a single EKF instance) will be started for each IMU specified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm-navigation-extended-kalman-filter-overview.rst:45
#: b28188c7ac964b3b95952036e00a7461
msgid "1: starts a single EKF core using the first IMU"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm-navigation-extended-kalman-filter-overview.rst:46
#: d0027f1390d24827975961e060f8776a
msgid "2: starts a single EKF core using only the second IMU"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm-navigation-extended-kalman-filter-overview.rst:47
#: 1f4323a1d763444d8088340ef021fce6
msgid "3: starts two separate EKF cores using the first and second IMUs respectively"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm-navigation-extended-kalman-filter-overview.rst:49
#: b43ccf40f5344a2d8356957d3e24b5de
msgid ":ref:`EK3_PRIMARY<EK3_PRIMARY>`: selects which \"core\" or \"lane\" is used as the primary. A value of 0 selects the first IMU lane in the :ref:`EK3_IMU_MASK <EK3_IMU_MASK>`, 1 the second, etc. Be sure that the selected primary lane exists. See Affinity and Lane Switching below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm-navigation-extended-kalman-filter-overview.rst:53
#: 0cec4da3abe54d8b9f2a0aa8727e9ccd
msgid "Plane and Rover will fall back from EKF2 or EKF3 to DCM if the EKF becomes unhealthy or the EKF is not fusing GPS data despite the GPS having 3D Lock. There is no fallback from EKF3 to EKF2 (or EKF2 to EKF1)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm-navigation-extended-kalman-filter-overview.rst:58
#: fc964b0035a14e14bcf96baf5c8a07d0
msgid "Using the parameters above it is possible to run up to 5 AHRSs in parallel at the same time (DCMx1, EKF2x2, EKF3x2) but this can result in performance problems so if running EKF2 and EKF3 in parallel, set the IMU_MASK to reduce the total number of cores."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm-navigation-extended-kalman-filter-overview.rst:61
#: 50273cddd67641e3b705cacb1058c80e
msgid "Affinity and Lane Switching"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm-navigation-extended-kalman-filter-overview.rst:63
#: a753d8344bcb422792f89b3ec51a2a48
msgid "EKF3 provides the feature of sensor affinity which allows the EKF cores to also use non-primary instances of sensors, specifically, Airspeed, Barometer, Compass (Magnetometer) and GPS. This allows the vehicle to better manage good quality sensors and be able to switch lanes accordingly to use the best-performing one for state estimation. For more details and configuration, refer :ref:`EKF3 Affinity and Lane Switching <common-ek3-affinity-lane-switching>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm-navigation-extended-kalman-filter-overview.rst:66
#: e84004e4c0e74181a63672e992bf98d7
msgid "GPS / Non-GPS Transitions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm-navigation-extended-kalman-filter-overview.rst:68
#: 221fe1183ecb488ba7b4885b70e83417
msgid "EKF3 supports in-flight switching of sensors which can be useful for transitioning between GPS and Non-GPS environments.  See :ref:`GPS / Non-GPS Transitions <common-non-gps-to-gps>` for more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm-navigation-extended-kalman-filter-overview.rst:71
#: 48fc3b30386841e68c947cf3295ca4a8
msgid "Commonly modified parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm-navigation-extended-kalman-filter-overview.rst:73
#: c0bbb5658c6849859fb4cad308c4e086
msgid "EKF sensor sources, see :ref:`common-ekf-sources`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm-navigation-extended-kalman-filter-overview.rst:75
#: e88ab46067374c2bb368835a600251b6
msgid ":ref:`EK3_ALT_M_NSE <dev:extended-kalman-filter_ekf_alt_noise>`: Default is \"1.0\".  Lower number reduces reliance on accelerometers, increases reliance on barometer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm-navigation-extended-kalman-filter-overview.rst:77
#: 76e1a0a2d9ea4c91821e45d76c5a3dd5
msgid ":ref:`EK3_GPS_TYPE <dev:extended-kalman-filter_ekf_gps_type>`: Controls how GPS is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm-navigation-extended-kalman-filter-overview.rst:80
#: 8d517e8101124bb0b7906ab1030a496d
msgid "0 : use 3D velocity & 2D position from GPS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm-navigation-extended-kalman-filter-overview.rst:81
#: c4c01a4c76c744a4960698c05d77ec66
msgid "1 : use 2D velocity & 2D position (GPS velocity does not contribute to altitude estimate)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm-navigation-extended-kalman-filter-overview.rst:83
#: 7209906988dc4682a135befe04104f1d
msgid "2: use 2D position"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm-navigation-extended-kalman-filter-overview.rst:84
#: 0f30a3b5ef774c06952cb3d4cc294c35
msgid "3 : no GPS (will use :ref:`optical flow <copter:common-optical-flow-sensors-landingpage>` only if available)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm-navigation-extended-kalman-filter-overview.rst:86
#: b5c5ccefa5dc4b409aece6905f1aeda1
msgid ":ref:`EK3_YAW_M_NSE <EK3_YAW_M_NSE>`: Controls the weighting between GPS and Compass when calculating the heading.  Default is \"0.5\", lower values will cause the compass to be trusted more (i.e. higher weighting to the compass)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm-navigation-extended-kalman-filter-overview.rst:88
#: 9a8b8ca2ebfb47428fd39ecbf33808ce
msgid "As mentioned above, a more detailed overview of EKF theory and tuning parameters is available on the developer wiki's :ref:`Extended Kalman Filter Navigation Overview and Tuning <dev:extended-kalman-filter>`."
msgstr ""
